WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Two figures stand hand
in hand at a doorway.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.020
One half turns to leave, then turns back.

3
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.200
"Remember me when I am
gone away," she says.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.960
Then she asks again.

5
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.300
And again.

6
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.400
Then, at line 9, one small
word changes the request:

7
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:24.010
"Yet if you should forget me for a while"
Eight lines begging to be remembered,

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.730
and then, it's all right to forget.

9
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.430
Why the change?

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.260
In this mission, you'll
see how Christina Rossetti,

11
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.450
aged 18, talks about death
in the gentlest words.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.790
You'll count how often she
repeats that one word, remember.

13
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.460
And you'll find the sonnet's
turn, and what it changes.

14
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: work out why
she asks him to forget.
